BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Depth Leathercraft Intro - Sept 13 [Sundays - 4 week program]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T170000
UID:ttl-11048239890625@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Leatherworking at TTLMakerspace \n\n \n \n \n \n \n Learn the 
 basics of leather working at the TTL Makerspace in a small hands-on class 
 where we will study traditional as well as modern methods of working with 
 leather.\n\n \n \n \n \n Small class sizes will allow you to get the guida
 nce needed to get you making leather projects with confidence. You will ta
 ke home 4 creations of your own design and if you cant get enough in class
 \, you can use the TTL Makerspace leatherworking kits or borrow one of the
  Toronto Tool Library’s similar kits.\n\n Materials and equipment for al
 l projects are provided with the course.\n\n \n \n \n Projects: \n \n Proj
 ect 1: Leather Wallet \n Project 2: Coin Purse \n Project 3: Waterskin \n 
 Project 4: Collar/bracelet \n \n \n Materials and equipment for all projec
 ts are provided with the course. \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n\n \n Schedule \n4 
 weeks\, Sundays 2pm to 5pm \n \n \n\n \n \n Outcomes \n At the end of the 
 course you will have achieved the following goals: \n \n  \n\n \n- A good
  understanding of the nature and properties of leather \n\n- A solid found
 ation in various methods of cutting\, burnishing\, dying and finishing. \n
 \n- Experience with stamping and engraving leather projects. \n\n- Familia
 rity with sewing machines and their use on thinner leather. \n\n- Knowledg
 e of wet molding and the waterproofing of leather. \n\n- An understanding 
 of studs\, buckles\, rivets\, snaps and other hardware. \n\n \n \n \n \n\n
  \n Useful for: bags\, garments\, belts\, custom cases/sheaths
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-leathercraft-intro-sept-13-sun
 days-4-week-program
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Interactive Electronics Sept 10 [6 weeks\, Thursdays]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260910T210000
UID:ttl-11048225374401@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Jump into Electronics! \n\n In this course at TTLMakerspace\, 
 you will go from beginner to understanding the basic principles of electro
 nics\, working with components\, micro-controllers\, and programming for e
 xperiential electronics using light\, sound\, and motion.\n\n \n \n \n Wor
 kshop Schedule : \n Thursdays\, 6pm to 9pm (3 hours) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 
 Outcomes : \n \n \n \n \n At the end of this course you will have achieved
  the following goals: \n\n \n- \n A grasp of the various active and passiv
 e components used in electronics \n\n- \n Knowledge of analog and digital 
 sensors \n\n- \n Understanding of power supplies and electronic circuits \
 n\n- \n Use of soldering equipment \n\n- \n Programming micro-controllers 
 in Python \n\n- \n Communication protocols \n\n- \n Networking for connect
 ed devices \n\n \n Following this course\, you’ll be welcome to join the
  growing community of creators and makers at TTLMakerspace for continued s
 upport and encouragement in your electronics journey. \n\n \n \n \n Useful
  for: internet-of-things\, installations\, reactive lighting\, motorized d
 evices \n \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? 
  \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/interactive-electronics-sept-10-6-weeks
 -thursdays
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Game Design Comprehensive Sept 29 [6 weeks\, Tuesdays]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T210000
UID:ttl-11006607327425@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:Game Design Quick-start \n\n In this course at TTLMakerspace\,
  you will go from beginner to a working knowledge of game design and devel
 opment using the open-source engine Godot. \n\n Starting with the basics o
 f the game engine\, you’ll learn how to progress from a knowledge of gam
 e mechanics to a coherent\, engaging game experience. \n\n \n \n \n Worksh
 op Schedule : \n Mondays\, 6pm to 9pm (3 hours) \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Outco
 mes : \n \n \n \n \n At the end of this course you will have achieved the 
 following goals: \n\n \n- \n A grasp of planning out fun game-play mechani
 cs \n\n- \n Familiarity with features of the Godot Game Engine \n\n- \n Pr
 actical knowledge of animation techniques \n\n- \n Application of physics 
 for game-play mechanics \n\n- \n Comfort with 2D game development \n\n- \n
  Ability to publish and show your game \n\n- \n Working understanding of U
 I in games \n\n \n Following this course\, you’ll be welcome to join the
  growing community of creators and game developers at TTLMakerspace for co
 ntinued support and encouragement in your game development journey. \n\n \
 n \n \n Useful for: games\, art\, installations\, animation\, interactive 
 experiences \n \n \n \n \n Want to get notified next time classes are post
 ed?  \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/game-design-comprehensive-aug-4-6-weeks
 -tuesdays
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:In Depth Sewing Intro - Sept 29 [Tuesdays - 6 week program]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T210000
UID:ttl-11048175239361@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:LEARN TO SEW \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Suitable for beginners. T
 his class goes over the basics of operating a sewing machine\, cutting and
  sewing garments\, and basic pattern alterations. \n \n \n The main projec
 t for this class is an apron custom fit to YOU. A typical first project is
  a tote bag\,but we’ve chosen to have our students make an apron as it c
 overs the same skills while also teaching basic tailoring and fitting. The
  goal of this class is to provide students with the basic skills associate
 d with sewing\, understanding patterns\, and textiles\, while promoting co
 nfidence and shifting the mindset of your everyday clothing as things that
  suit your needs and body\, rather than things to simply wear. \n \n \n \n
  \n \n\n \n \n This class will also explore clothing repairs and minor alt
 erations like hemming\, altering\nnecklines\, adding pockets\, etc. Studen
 ts are encouraged to bring in items they wish to alter or repair. \n \n \
 n Materials and equipment for all projects are provided with the course. \
 n \n \n\n \n Schedule \n6 weeks\, Tuesdays 6pm to 9pm \n \n \n\n \n \n Out
 comes \n At the end of the course you will have achieved the following goa
 ls: \n \n \n- Proficiency with operating a sewing machine safely \n\n- Und
 erstanding of fabric types\, their uses\, how to prep them for sewing\, an
 d how to cut fabric \n\n- Comfort with taking measurements of the body and
  how to apply them to a pattern \n\n- Knowledge of basic pattern alteratio
 ns and how to adjust existing garments to fit you better \n\n- Understandi
 ng of how to transfer patterns to fabric so that space is used as efficien
 tly as possible \n\n- Understanding of pinning and ironing techniques \n\n
 - Familiarity with basic sewing techniques including seams\, hemming\, han
 d stitching\,\napplying pockets\, fasteners including buttons\, zippers\, 
 snaps\, and ties\, as well as\ndifferent stitch uses for different techniq
 ues and materials\n\n- Basic repairs like fixing holes\, torn seams\, hole
 s in pockets\, adding patches\n\n- Basic alterations like adjusting hems\,
  changing necklines\, switching out buttons or other fasteners
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/in-depth-sewing-intro-sept-29-tuesdays-
 6-week-program
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Laser for Artists - Sept 12 [Saturdays 6 week comprehensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260912T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260912T170000
UID:ttl-11041171833025@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:In this course at TTLMakerspace\, you will go from beginner to
  practical working knowledge of designing and modelling in 2D and 3D\, and
  the operation of a laser for etching and cutting a variety of materials. 
 \n\n Starting with desktop versions of lasers you’ll work your way throu
 gh lessons and projects up to the industrial ThunderLaser cutter. \n\n Out
 comes: \n\n At the end of this course you will have achieved the following
  goals: \n\n \n- A complete understanding of the steps needed to go from c
 oncept to completed project \n\n- Familiarity with the properties of a var
 iety of materials - woods\, plastics\, textiles \n\n- Experience and compr
 ehension of the most important principles of CAD modelling for constructin
 g with laser cut parts \n\n- Setting speeds and power levels \n\n- Creatin
 g a design environment and workflow \n\n- Full understanding of the most c
 ommon etching and cutting operations \n\n- Experience creating tool paths 
 with Lightburn software \n\n- Setting up materials and performing operatio
 ns \n\n- Machine maintenance and Safety \n\n \n Schedule: 6 lessons\, Satu
 rdays\, 2pm-5pm \n\n Following this course\, you’ll be certified to use 
 desktop lasers\, and book time with the industrial laser at TTLMakerspace 
 (with your membership). You will also be able to join the growing communit
 y of TTL Makers sharing Laser knowledge on our Discord community. \n\n Use
 ful for : signs\, gifts\, personalising anything\, stamp-making\, organise
 r\, decorative items\, lanterns \n\n Want to get notified next time classe
 s are posted? \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/designing-for-lasers-sept-12-saturdays-
 6-week-comprehensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Practical 3D Print Sept 21 [Mondays - 6 Week Comprehensive]
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260921T210000
UID:ttl-11048171536577@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:In this course at TTLMakerspace\, you will go beyond basic 3D 
 printing knowledge and be able to create custom designs. Learn to use CAD 
 modelling to upgrade or build your own models\, optimized for 3D print.\n\
 n \n \n \n \n \n \n Starting with manual printer control\, you will progre
 ss to custom modelling and even advanced techniques such as 3D scanning an
 d reverse engineering.\n\n Schedule: \n\n \n Six three-hour weekly classes
 \, Mondays 6:00pm to 9:00pm.\n\n \n \n \n \n \n Outcomes: \n \n \n At the 
 end of this course you will have achieved the following goals: \n \n \n \n
 - A complete understanding of the steps needed to go from concept to compl
 eted part\n\n- Experience and comprehension of parametric 3D modelling\n\n
 - Knowledge of 3D printing best practices \n\n- Familiarity with scanning
  for 3D print \n\n- Principles of reverse engineering and part repair\n\n
 - Understanding of the properties of different 3D printing filaments\n\n- 
 Use cases for SLA (resin) printing vs. FDM printing \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \
 n \n Following this hands-on course\, you’ll be certified to use 3D prin
 ters and book time with the machines at the TTLMakerspace (with your membe
 rship). You will also be able to join the growing community of TTL Makers 
 sharing 3D printing & 3D modelling knowledge on our Discord community.\n\n
  Useful for: design prototyping\, custom organizational tools\, repairs\, 
 prop-making\, decorations\, fabrication tools\n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \n \
 n Want to get notified next time classes are posted? \n\n Join our mailing
  list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/practical-3d-print-sept-21-mondays-6-we
 ek-comprehensive
X-SOURCE:Toronto Tool Library
END:VEVENT
