UID:ttl-11048167833793@ttlmarket.com
DESCRIPTION:CNC for Artists \n\n \n \n\n \n In this course at TTLMakerspac
 e\, you will learn the technical aspects of using modern digital fabricati
 on techniques with a CNC mill for artistic expression. \n \n \n \n \n \n \
 n Starting with desktop versions of CNC machines\, you’ll work your way 
 through lessons up to the industrial Omni 1350 6’ x 8’ CNC milling mac
 hine. \n \n \n\n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Schedule : \n \n \n Six thr
 ee-hour weekly classes\, Mondays 6pm to 9pm. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Outcomes
  : \n \n \n At the end of this course you will have achieved the following
  goals: \n \n \n- \n Understanding of how to design for the strengths of a
  CNC mill \n\n- \n Familiarity with the properties of a variety of hardwoo
 d materials \n\n- \n Experience with constructive structural geometry \n\n
 - \n Using a vector design tool \n\n- \n Creating decorative inlays with v
 eneer \n\n- \n 3-dimensional surfaces for decorative wall-art \n\n- \n 3D 
 surface milling \n\n- \n Machine maintenance and Safety \n\n \n \n Followi
 ng this course\, you’ll be certified to use desktop mills\, and book tim
 e with the industrial mill at TTLMakerspace (with your membership). You wi
 ll also be able to join the growing community of TTL Makers sharing CNC kn
 owledge on our Discord community. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n Useful for: inlays\
 , wall-art\, sculptural designs\, lighting \n \n \n\n \n \n Want to get no
 tified next time classes are posted? \n\n Join our mailing list!
LOCATION:TTLMakerspace\, 192 Spadina Ave.\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://ttlmarket.com/products/cnc-milling-for-artists-sept-21-mondays
